# The Deck (playable variant) — NEVINYRRAL'S DISK INSTEAD OF CHAOS ORB.
#   That is the whole difference from the list this is taken from, and it
#   is the reason this file exists: without it The Deck cannot be played
#   here at all.
#
#   It ships under "Playable variants" rather than with the community
#   lists because those folders are a provenance ledger — every entry a
#   deck somebody really published, each folder pinned by tests to the
#   number its sources yielded. This one is OURS, so it is counted
#   separately and says so.
#
# ONE CARD CHANGED, and it is not a
#   deckbuilding opinion. Randy Buehler's August 2015 Old School list
#   (os_the_deck_buehler_2015.deck) is 59/60 implementable in this pool;
#   the sixtieth is Chaos Orb, which no digital version of Magic has ever
#   implemented because playing it means physically flipping the card onto
#   the table. This project drops it by definition, with Falling Star,
#   Shahrazad and Word of Command (docs/ROADMAP.md — the same four s30
#   drops, and none of them is in cards/data/ at all).
#
#   The substitution is 1 Chaos Orb -> 1 Nevinyrral's Disk: the nearest
#   thing in the pool to the job Chaos Orb did in this deck, which was to
#   be the answer to a permanent nothing else in the list could answer.
#   It is slower and symmetrical, so this is NOT Buehler's deck and is not
#   labelled as though it were — the original stays beside it, unchanged
#   and unplayable, because a reference list you can trust is worth more
#   than a playable one you cannot.
#
# archetype: The Deck — Old School 93/94, made playable
# designer: Randy Buehler (list); the one substitution is this project's
# year: August 2015 (list), 2026-09-06 (substitution)
# source: os_the_deck_buehler_2015.deck, which carries the full provenance
# group: Playable variants
name: The Deck (playable variant)
